  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "-(close[t-1]/close[t-21]-1) / std(pct_change(close)[t-20:t-1]) * I(Q50(dispersion_252[t-1]) < dispersion[t-1] <= Q75(dispersion_252[t-1]))",
    "description": "Cross-sectional contrarian 20-trading-day return scaled by trailing 20-day volatility. Signal is active in the intermediate cross-asset dispersion bucket, above the trailing 252-day median and at or below its trailing 75th percentile. All prices, dispersion statistics, and thresholds are lagged to avoid look-ahead. Dispersion is the cross-sectional standard deviation of one-day returns."
